    {
      "atom_id": "atom::307ba8b829e2c5c2fed7647d",
      "source_handle": "P0573",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "research_scope"
      ],
      "value": "The review focuses on the integration of fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) with immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) for cancer treatment. It covers clinical evidence from various solid tumors (melanoma, colorectal cancer, etc.), preclinical mechanistic studies, and optimization strategies for FMT protocols.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fdaeb367f0c12dababc11cbf52f70b451762bf8bc2",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c7f920cea77ba135b6eb8184f6ac26c844bb27ccc",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::d1590c0e09f64bdeb0f7b69bc925181bb5bf6cf12262b59e2e52cbc9f99d8e7c",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "atom_id": "atom::1bdd4c29ead36b61ef77d66e",
      "source_handle": "P0573",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "work_summary"
      ],
      "value": "This is a comprehensive narrative review that critically examines the controversial effects of combining FMT with ICIs. It synthesizes evidence from clinical trials and preclinical studies to explain why FMT sometimes enhances ICI efficacy while other times shows no benefit or adverse effects. The paper outlines mechanisms involving gut microbiota modulation, metabolite profiles, and tumor microenvironment changes, and discusses factors influencing outcomes such as donor selection, recipient characteristics, and administration protocols. It concludes by proposing future research directions including large-scale trials, multi-omics integration, and alternative microbiome-based therapies.",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::7370217b0d1083d4f465a9fdaeb367f0c12dababc11cbf52f70b451762bf8bc2",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        },
        {
          "record_id": "record::b8f4ede79d64928928c3569c7f920cea77ba135b6eb8184f6ac26c844bb27ccc",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        },
